/tmp/tmp.GrURyZYBlb/src/Puzzles.tex:52:The computational complexity of pencil puzzles has attracted considerable interest for their rich connection to constraint satisfaction and graph theory. Many popular pencil puzzles have been proved to be NP-complete using various techniques, including Five Cells \cite{fivecells}, Goishi Hiroi \cite{goishi}, Hashiwokakero \cite{bridges}, Herugolf \cite{makaro}, Heyawake \cite{heyawake}, Kakuro \cite{sudoku}, Makaro \cite{makaro}, Numberlink \cite{numberlink}, Slitherlink \cite{sudoku}, Sudoku \cite{sudoku}, Sumplete \cite{sumplete}, Tatamibari \cite{tatamibari}, Tilepaint \cite{fivecells}, and Zeiger \cite{zeiger}.
