Before final handoff I’m doing one additional, unrequired attack motivated by the tightened G4 model: start from a complementary perfect matching and greedily flip 2×2 domino pairs whenever that merges alternating cycles. This checks whether the “many local cycles versus one tour” obstacle collapses under an obvious cycle-merging heuristic that the original three attacks did not cover.
